## 3. Analysis of Items #9 (`skip_barrier`) and #10 (Wave/LDS Occupancy A/B)

- **Item #9 (`skip_barrier` outside `flow`)**:
  - In `Engine::record_net` (`gpu/src/engine.cpp:567-572`), the only two independent consecutive dispatches (`pooled_history2` writing `pdst_` and `ae` writing `expo_[cur]`/`blk_`) already omit the UAV barrier between them (`d.barrier()` is issued only after `ae`).
  - All other dispatches outside the 10-kernel `enc2..dec2_1` flow chain (`enc0_attr -> enc0_stage_32_64 -> enc1`, and `dec2_1 -> dec1_0 -> dec1_1 -> dec0_0 -> dec0_1 -> post -> downsample`) have strict full-tensor RAW dependencies on the immediately preceding kernel's output buffer; skipping any of those UAV barriers would cause data races.
- **Item #10 (Top-5 hottest dispatches & Fast `_lt` vs Legacy `_f` A/B)**:
  - At both 1080p Quality (`1280x720 -> 1920x1080`) and 4K Quality (`2560x1440 -> 3840x2160`), the Top-5 dispatches account for ~53.5%–55.9% of total GPU time: `enc0_stage_32_64` (~12.4–12.8%), `post` (~11.4–12.6%), `dec_up_32_64_64` (~10.7–11.1%), `dec_head_32_64` (~10.4–10.7%), and `enc_stage_64_64_96` (~8.6–8.7%).
  - Enabling the `_lt` (`LT_Q16` / `LT_FP8_2X` / `LT_TILE32`) kernel set + `flow` (4 row-completion replicas + 16 all-done replicas + SALU LCG backoff) reduces 1080p steady-state median GPU time from `3.445 ms` (`Legacy _f+flow`) to `3.123 ms` (`Fast _lt+flow`, **-9.3%**).
